{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_26a3cb98ff4cdd901a66252b198b2a330bcb13341a0b6ee95eb9e61acc711143"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: PRs require conventional-commit titles, a Problem/Cause/Change/Verification body, before/after images for UI changes, and one concern per PR."},{"claim_ids":["clm_371dbe999fffc43586ceb731c6e0f7127169cd9a15471601d1c40e20a4fbe90c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: AGENTS.md defines a five-stage dev loop (/context, /quality, /test, /ship plus utilities) implemented as agent skills under .agents/skills/, with /ship wrapping an autonomous PR-to-merge playbook."},{"claim_ids":["clm_43718c723c662d9363f9bac9c02387d673d9097229f989d4643de9a45f1c205d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: Node.js 22.x is required because node:sqlite is the primary database engine, and each app under apps/ has independent node_modules with no npm workspaces."},{"claim_ids":["clm_86c97dce700ad06af87539ba3420dc4f7ce2ceae3803f6ed57a648725d74f707"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: releases are cut by tagging main with vX.Y.Z, triggering a workflow that publishes a draft GitHub Release; Windows builds are gated behind the ADE_WINDOWS_PUBLIC_RELEASE_ENABLED variable."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e2d3c884f44e5bd60f5b2f4685dc485d194085cb4c761bfabb917e00970e6a09"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: validation uses desktop and CLI typecheck/test/build commands, with the large desktop suite sharded and the smallest relevant subset run first."}],"claim_ids":["clm_26a3cb98ff4cdd901a66252b198b2a330bcb13341a0b6ee95eb9e61acc711143","clm_371dbe999fffc43586ceb731c6e0f7127169cd9a15471601d1c40e20a4fbe90c","clm_43718c723c662d9363f9bac9c02387d673d9097229f989d4643de9a45f1c205d","clm_86c97dce700ad06af87539ba3420dc4f7ce2ceae3803f6ed57a648725d74f707","clm_e2d3c884f44e5bd60f5b2f4685dc485d194085cb4c761bfabb917e00970e